This package builds the CUDA runtime, without model weights or the npm web UI.
Use an OpenAI-compatible client with llama-kvmem-server.
The patched llama/ggml libraries are statically linked into the two tools, so
this package can coexist with sci-misc/llama-cpp and prism-llama-cpp.

For RTX 5080, select the architecture in /etc/portage/env/kvmem-llama-cpp:
    CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES="120a-real"
and add to /etc/portage/package.env:
    sci-misc/kvmem-llama-cpp kvmem-llama-cpp

Download Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-mtp.gguf separately from:
https://huggingface.co/ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-GGUF

The upstream 16 GiB IQ3 recipe uses a bounded GPU KV working set with a
256K logical context. Historical KV is stored in system RAM. Start with:
    llama-kvmem-server -m /path/to/Qwen3.8-27B-GSQ-RCO-IQ3_S-mtp.gguf \
        --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18200 -c 262144 --gpu-layers all \
        --kvmem-budget 36864 --kvmem-gen-reserve 16384 \
        -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 --spec-type draft-mtp --no-ui

Check the upstream README for current sampling and memory settings. A single
generation, including reasoning, must fit --kvmem-gen-reserve. Model inference
correctness must be checked after changing the CUDA compiler; a successful
build alone does not validate IQ3 output.
